  "discussion": "Tiny surf along north-facing shores will persist through today. A small northwest swell will arrive Thursday giving a small bump Thursday afternoon and Friday. This will then be followed by a slightly larger medium-period north-northwest swell this weekend. A potential storm-force low in the process of developing north of Japan could send a larger long period west-northwest swell early next week. This swell is still uncertain and will depend on the evolution of the developing low. South shores will remain small before a series of moderate, south- southwesterly swells boost surf heights near to above seasonal average this weekend into early next week. Rough trade wind swell will gradually decline later today as trade winds decrease, leading to a slight reduction in surf through the remainder of the week. A small, medium-period east swell is possible Thursday into the weekend that will help keep surf elevated for east-facing shores.",
